{"assets":["/editorial-assets/763af577a00da62a82631cb74d62aaf14c83fc31bc80187062b2ac334ce11b2f.png","/editorial-assets/73c7dc826d51ab382f31c61c383564289a439655c23002ed12310683645c4ab7.png","/editorial-assets/0f581565b287d6644883c30dba32c4eb508f4e0470955e1b6439dca971509f9b.png","/editorial-assets/15ea70e2d9a77e074cd0fad1e0efc2a75a2a0f44242fb83a25f9b36348e22dbf.png","/editorial-assets/176b4d6b2082a742b79e6ed20d7e1ed7782d78b1c72c73d3132043d8fc382e87.png","/editorial-assets/d00424a0195e916079bff82e7582d194be1689c874fc11814a86a7e8aaa55ef0.png","/editorial-assets/9e44c8d9dc4f5ffcf2fb969887bd16e0835c721311867c582d4c73f18a2979c1.png","/editorial-assets/ba3d1b6c1dca07ff6dc6b39bf92627813ddb7fc5d531236a733138b5d4991cd8.png","/editorial-assets/58018141f7a33a7a67f2fa108ee95feda14991ead779d5ddb6d94faf243308cd.png","/editorial-assets/f66c5c939d1367537c0e1c7e7e72f5ee6fa8ef091d2b3b289b915492dc700afd.png"],"contestId":"185","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No problem was specially taken from \"Wikipedia\". For me it's really hard to understand, that problem \"B\" was there."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A (Div 2)."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" (Idea : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Gerald"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gerald"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", realization : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", code : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/186/submission/1670635"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1670635"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the lengths of 2 strings aren't equal — that means \"NO\". We try to find the positions in strings, where chars are different. If there 1 or more than 2 such positions — \"NO\". After that we swap 2 characters in the first string, and check for their equality."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B (Div 2)."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" (Idea : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", realization : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", code : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/186/submission/1670637"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1670637"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can see, that we can do all in integers, because k is integer number of percent."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each dwarf we should find his optimal strategy — to check 2 strategies with speed."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We should sort them."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A (Div 1)."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" (Idea : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", realization : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", code : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/185/submission/1652592"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1652592"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":") Let's propose, that after the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th year, there is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" triangles up and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" triangles down. After another iteration we can see, that amount of triangles became — 3"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" up and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 3"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" down. Let's see the difference between them: at the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th it's "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and at the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1-th — it's (3"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") - ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 3"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") = 2 * ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). We can see, that difference between amount of triangles grown up by 2. Because on the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th year the difference became 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and all amount of triangles is 4"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". We can see, that on the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th year the number of our triangles is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/763af577a00da62a82631cb74d62aaf14c83fc31bc80187062b2ac334ce11b2f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". That can be computed by modulo p using the fast-power algorithm."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B (Div 1)."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" (Idea : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", realization : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", code : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/185/submission/1652597"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1652597"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":") This problem was made by my love to inequalities. :-)! The answer for this problem is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/73c7dc826d51ab382f31c61c383564289a439655c23002ed12310683645c4ab7.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Prove: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0f581565b287d6644883c30dba32c4eb508f4e0470955e1b6439dca971509f9b.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". (This is AM-GM inequality. "},{"attrs":{"href":"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Wiki/index.php/AM-GM"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Link for whom don't know it."}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The equality becomes only, when "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/15ea70e2d9a77e074cd0fad1e0efc2a75a2a0f44242fb83a25f9b36348e22dbf.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And you should check on zeroes. If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 0 — you can choose any good answer — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C (Div 1)."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" No comments. :-)!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D (Div 1)."}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" (Idea : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", realization : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/cerealguy"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cerealguy"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Gerald"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gerald"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", code : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/185/submission/1652604"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1652604"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is number theory problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I'm trying to explain it step by step:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1) Let's prove, that LCD is maximum 2."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/176b4d6b2082a742b79e6ed20d7e1ed7782d78b1c72c73d3132043d8fc382e87.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Squaring both sides we get "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/d00424a0195e916079bff82e7582d194be1689c874fc11814a86a7e8aaa55ef0.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", but we want to "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/9e44c8d9dc4f5ffcf2fb969887bd16e0835c721311867c582d4c73f18a2979c1.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". This means, that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be only 2."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2) Let's make this lenghty product simplier."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ba3d1b6c1dca07ff6dc6b39bf92627813ddb7fc5d531236a733138b5d4991cd8.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can count this by modulo "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" fast, and divide it by 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is odd."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3) There is many interesting things in this solution."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Firstly, it doesn't work, when "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2 — but it can easily done by you."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The other problem is harder, what if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/58018141f7a33a7a67f2fa108ee95feda14991ead779d5ddb6d94faf243308cd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", this means that for each "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/f66c5c939d1367537c0e1c7e7e72f5ee6fa8ef091d2b3b289b915492dc700afd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", and this mean,"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"that for each "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≥ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 ≡ "},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"2. And the product by modulo "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E (Div. 1) (Idea : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Aksenov239"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aksenov239"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", relization : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/cerealguy"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cerealguy"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", code : "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/185/submission/1652611"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1652611"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This problem wasn't taken to ROI, because of that I gave it here. This is pretty hard problem. I can't now realize, what "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/cerealguy"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cerealguy"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" wrote, but his solution is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nlogn"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") — without binary search. For me it's quite hard to understand, because my first solution was with binary search. And there were solutions, that has a worse asymptothic, but they run faster."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Because of that I can only give you key ideas, that can help you. (afterwards you can see the code of "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/cerealguy"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cerealguy"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ideas:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's find for each person the nearest subway point for them. It can be done in nlogn with use of segment tree or something else."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can see, that if one person goes to subway, the others, which distance to subway is smaller, can go to subway too — it doesn't affect the answer. Because of that we sort all persons by their distanse to subway."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The area of the person, where he can come in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" seconds, is romb. And we can intersect all rombes in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the intersection is like rectangle."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's make the first intersection. When nobody goes to subway. We get a rectangle."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The main idea, that for this rectangle — the nearest subway becomes always the same. We go throught people in sorted order, we can fast recalculate this small rectangle — and because of that we can fast recalculate the answer."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And we get a solution in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nlogn"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") time. Ta-dams."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thank you all for your attention. I'm deeply sorry about the problem \"C\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/4488"}